nomics and the School of Management at Yale University. He received his B.A. from Trinity College, Cambridge University, his M.A. from Northwestern University, and his Ph.D. from Harvard University. A specialist in microeconomic theory and economic history, he has published in <em>Economic Letters</em>, <em>Journal of Economic Theory</em>, <em>Journal of Economic History</em>, <em>Journal of Legal Studies</em>, <em>Journal of Theoretical and Institutional Economics</em>, and <em>Econometrica</em>. His current projects include \"Generalized Utilitarianism and Harsanyi's Impartial Observer Theorem\" and \"Mean-Dispersion Preferences.\"</p> </p></div></div>  </div>\n\n    </div>\n  \n          </div>\n</div>\n\n  </div>\n\n  </div>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\n\t\t<div class=\"content-bottom\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t</main>\n\n\t<footer class=\"footer\" role=\"contentinfo\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"footer__inner\">\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"footer__logo-txt\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"topper-logo\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"http://www.yale.edu\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYale\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t<div class=\"footer__statements\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"footer__menu-links\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<nav role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"block-yale-oyc-footer-menu\" id=\"block-yale-oyc-footer\" class=\"block block-menu navigation menu--footer\">\n            \n  <h2 class=\"visually-hidden\" id=\"block-yale-oyc-footer-menu\">Footer</h2>\n  \n\n        \n              <ul class=\"menu\">\n                    <li class=\"menu-item\">\n        <a href=\"https://usability.yale.edu/web-accessibility/accessibility-yale\">Accessibility at Yale</a>\n              </li>\n                <li class=\"menu-item\">\n        <a href=\"https://privacy.yale.edu/resources/privacy-statement\">Privacy policy</a>\n              </li>\n        </ul>\n  \n\n\n  </nav>\n\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"footer__copyright\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\